      "v": 6,
      "zh": "按我们所得的恩赐，各有不同。或说预言，就当照着信心的程度说预言；",
      "en": "And we have different gifts[NOTE:1] according to the grace given to us. If the gift is prophecy, that individual must use it in proportion to his faith.[NOTE:2]",
      "notes": [
        "This word comes from the same root as “grace” in the following clause; it means “things graciously given,” “grace-gifts.”",
        "The last part of this verse has no verb; either an indicative or imperative is implied. Most likely an imperative is intended because of the general tenor of this section of the epistle as exhortation and because of the particular flow of this verse, which seems to imply how to use spiritual gifts."
      ],
